{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The NPC has developed an ambitious “Economic Justice through Economic Education Project” that aims to train grassroots activists, including DSAers, to critique neoliberal ideology and put forth a progressive alternative economic policy.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The “Economic Justice through Economic Education Project” will create “workshops in a box” that can be readily duplicated by DSA local activists around three major themes: the causes of the current economic crisis, an explanation and critique of neoliberal ideology and policy proposals from the perspective of ordinary people and the environmental future, and feasible progressive policy proposals that would redress economic stagnation, mass unemployment, and foreclosures.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Workshops created by the “Economic Justice through Economic Education Project” will incorporate a socialist-feminist analysis of how capitalism intersects with other forms of oppression.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA commits to taking the Economic Justice through Economic Education Project on the road to train activists to be popular “tribunes” against neoliberal orthodoxy.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA will approach coalition partners in community and labor organizations to join this project to build an “alternative critical sense” to the bankrupt “common sense” of neoliberalism.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The convention endorses the NPC’s efforts to create a significant educational and political project around the 50th Anniversary of The Other America and Michael Harrington’s role in initiating the War on Poverty.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

